<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S1.F1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Learning and Final Vote Visualization.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.2 </span>Related Work</h3>

<section id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generalizations of the Condorcet Jury Theorem.</h4>

<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Extensions of the CJT typically either allow for more general voting rules or weaken the <em id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">homogeneity</em> or <em id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">independence</em> assumption, thereby extending the <em id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">asymptotic guarantee</em> of the CJT.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeauthor"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">List and Goodin</a></cite> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeyear"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">2001</a></cite>) generalized the result to <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">plurality voting</span> over multiple alternatives, while <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeauthor"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Everaere et al.</a></cite> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeyear"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">2010</a></cite>) extended it to <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">approval voting</span>, assuming that the probability of approving the correct alternative exceeds that of any incorrect one.
Crucially for our work, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeauthor"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Owen et al.</a></cite> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeyear"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">1989</a></cite>) relaxed the homogeneity assumption, proving that convergence requires only that the <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">average</span> reliability of the group exceeds 0.5.
Other works have addressed independence by introducing an <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">opinion leader</span>, swaying the electorate towards one of the alternatives <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>, or limiting pairwise correlations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we likewise generalize the CJT by (1) extending the one-shot decision model to a <em id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sequential setting</em>, (2) permitting <em id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">heterogeneous agents</em>, (3) whose decisions can <em id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">depend on their previous choices</em>, and (4) allowing agents to <em id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">abstain</em> from voting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Delegation and Liquid Democracy.</h4>

<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Permitting agents to abstain can be viewed as delegating their vote to the remaining group. This connects to <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">liquid democracy</span>, where agents transitively delegate votes to those deemed more capable.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, there is a critical distinction to the framework proposed here. Standard liquid democracy models constrain delegation to <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">local social ties</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeauthor"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kahng et al.</a></cite> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeyear"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">2021</a></cite>) prove that such local mechanisms cannot guarantee to outperform direct voting because they risk <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">weight concentration</span>, where a few proxies accumulate massive influence, destroying the independence required for the “wisdom of the crowd.”</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our framework avoids this failure mode by using <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">calibration-based abstention</span> rather than social delegation. Agents do not delegate to a specific neighbor; they effectively “delegate” to the collective mean by withdrawing their noise, keeping influence distributed among all confident agents.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contributions.</h4>

<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We develop a probabilistic framework for collective decision-making with calibrated abstention. Our main contributions are:
(1) A sequential decision model in which agents undergo a <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">confidence calibration</span> phase to estimate their own competence and <span id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">selectively participate</span> via a confidence gate;
(2) A generalization of the CJT to this sequential setting, proving asymptotic convergence for a heterogeneous, confidence-gated electorate; and
(3) A non-asymptotic lower bound on the probability of a correct majority.
(4) Finally, we demonstrate the utility of these bounds via Monte Carlo simulations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.3 </span>Motivational Scenario</h3>

<div id="S1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further motivate the framework proposed in this work, we briefly discuss its ties to the <em id="S1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hallucination problem</em> for Large Language Models (LLMs), a phenomenon in which they produce confident yet factually incorrect outputs. A recent OpenAI study by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeauthor"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kalai et al.</a></cite> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeyear"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">2025</a></cite>) argues that many LLM <span id="S1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">hallucinations</span> are ordinary <span id="S1.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">binary classification</span> errors: under binary grading (responses scored as simply correct vs. incorrect), systems are implicitly rewarded for guessing and penalized for abstaining, which can encourage confident yet wrong answers. They urge a shift in how we <span id="S1.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">evaluate and deploy</span> LLMs by introducing explicit confidence targets and granting credit for admitting not to know the answer (“IDK”) when uncertainty is high, so models answer only when sufficiently confident.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This presents a theoretical challenge: How can we aggregate agents who are incentivized to selectively abstain? We answer this with a probabilistic voting framework: agents undergo a calibration phase to learn their own competence, <span id="S1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">abstain unless confident</span>, and only the resulting “filtered” electorate votes at the final decision point. This operationalizes confidence-targeted evaluation and, via concentration bounds, yields probabilistic guarantees on the correctness of the group decision in <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and a bound on the probability for a group of agents hallucinating in <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 2 (Collective Hallucination Bound). ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In this context, our approach synthesizes three active lines of LLM research. First is <span id="S1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ensemble-style decoding</span>, most notably Self-Consistency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, which samples multiple reasoning paths (mimicking diverse agents) and aggregates answers to improve accuracy. Second is the tradition of <span id="S1.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">classification with a reject option</span>, ranging from Chow’s optimal abstention rule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> to modern deep selective prediction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>; our framework operationalizes this by treating agents as selective classifiers with calibrated refusal. Third, recent studies on <span id="S1.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LLM uncertainty</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> suggest models’ self-evaluated competence correlates with correctness. In our terms, an agent’s self-evaluated competence can serve as a prior in the calibration phase.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The Formal Voting Framework.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As the basic building blocks of our binary voting framework, let there be two alternatives,
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}=\{\omega^{*},{\omega_{\dagger}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}=\{\omega^{*},{\omega_{\dagger}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and encode <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\omega_{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\omega_{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a single decision instance, we denote the (a priori unknown) true world state by a random variable <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, our setting involves a sequence of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> tasks. Therefore, for each time step <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,\dots,T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,\dots,T\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{t}\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{t}\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the ground truth of the task at <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and we write <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}=(\Omega_{1},\dots,\Omega_{T})\in\mathcal{W}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}=(\Omega_{1},\dots,\Omega_{T})\in\mathcal{W}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> for the complete sequence of ground truths. Probabilities of internal private choices and public votes at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> are taken <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">conditional on</span> <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. When we say “under the true state,” we generally refer to the event <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\Omega_{t}=\omega^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Omega_{t}=\omega^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\Omega_{t}={\omega_{\dagger}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Omega_{t}={\omega_{\dagger}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>) for the current task.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{a_{1},\dots,a_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{a_{1},\dots,a_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of agents with <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N:=|\mathcal{A}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N:=|\mathcal{A}|</annotation></semantics></math>. A single majority-voting instance (e.g., the collective decision at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) is modeled as a partial function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v:\mathcal{A}\to\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v:\mathcal{A}\to\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> defined on the set of non-abstainers. The score of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#_{v}\,\omega:=|\{i\in\mathcal{A}:v(i)=\omega\}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>#</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#_{v}\,\omega:=|\{i\in\mathcal{A}:v(i)=\omega\}|</annotation></semantics></math>, and the winner is any <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> with strictly higher score than its competitor, thereby treating ties as non-wins <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Confidence Measure and Updating.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our model, every agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> faces a sequence of i.i.d. tasks from <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> time steps. Rounds <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,\dots,T-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,\dots,T-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> form a <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">learning phase</span> (agents receive feedback and update beliefs); round <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">decision phase</span> (only this round’s public votes are aggregated). We posit a fixed, unknown parameter <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> capturing <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">distribution-level reliability</em>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\ :=\ \mathbb{P}\big(\text{$a_{i}$ is correct on a random task from }\mathcal{D}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mtext> is correct on a random task from </mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\ :=\ \mathbb{P}\big(\text{$a_{i}$ is correct on a random task from }\mathcal{D}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the agent’s inherent <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">epistemic type</span> or domain-specific competence (e.g., a juror’s aptitude for interpreting evidence in a specific class of legal cases). Under the assumption that decision tasks are drawn i.i.d., <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a structural invariant; this implies that an agent’s past frequency of success is a valid signal for learning their own type, rather than a reflection of changing ability.
Equivalently, for each round <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the correctness indicator <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}\{X_{i,t}=\Omega_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}\{X_{i,t}=\Omega_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is Bernoulli(<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) and independent across <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (and across agents), conditional on <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the sequence of ground truths <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Omega_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Omega_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">average probability</span> of making the correct choice by <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The agent’s <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">probabilistic belief</span> about its true reliability <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by a random variable <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows a Beta distribution:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}\sim\text{Beta}(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}\sim\text{Beta}(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are the current shape parameters (often interpreted as pseudo-counts of correct and incorrect outcomes, respectively). These parameters are updated dynamically as the agent receives feedback on their choices in each binary decision problem.
The agent’s <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">confidence</span> in its reliability, denoted by <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, is derived from this belief, represented by the distribution of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the posterior probability that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than a critical probability threshold, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\text{critical},i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>critical</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\text{critical},i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}:=\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,t}&gt;{p_{\text{critical},i}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>critical</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}:=\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,t}&gt;{p_{\text{critical},i}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For example, for binary decisions, a natural choice for the critical probability threshold is <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\text{critical},i}}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>critical</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\text{critical},i}}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. In this context, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the agent’s belief that its true reliability <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. If, for instance, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}=0.65" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.65</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}=0.65</annotation></semantics></math>, it means the agent believes there is a <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="65\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>65</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">65\%</annotation></semantics></math> probability that its true reliability <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fundamentals of the Beta Distribution.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Beta distribution is a continuous probability distribution defined on the interval <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, parameterized by two positive shape parameters <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The probability density function (PDF) of the Beta distribution is given by:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x;\alpha,\beta)=\frac{x^{\alpha-1}(1-x)^{\beta-1}}{B(\alpha,\beta)},\quad x\in[0,1]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x;\alpha,\beta)=\frac{x^{\alpha-1}(1-x)^{\beta-1}}{B(\alpha,\beta)},\quad x\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\alpha,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\alpha,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Beta function</span>, a normalization constant defined as <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\alpha,\beta)=\int_{0}^{1}x^{\alpha-1}(1-x)^{\beta-1}\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\alpha,\beta)=\int_{0}^{1}x^{\alpha-1}(1-x)^{\beta-1}\,dx</annotation></semantics></math>. The parameters <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> can be interpreted as "pseudo-counts" of successes and failures, respectively, pulling the distribution toward 1 or 0 accordingly. When <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the Beta distribution reduces to the uniform distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At each decision instance at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, each agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> receives feedback on whether its private choice was correct. This feedback is used to update the parameters of its Beta belief distribution. If agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s current belief state is <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Beta}(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Beta}(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If agent <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s private decision at time <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">correct</span>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,t+1},\beta_{i,t+1})=(\alpha_{i,t}+1,\beta_{i,t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,t+1},\beta_{i,t+1})=(\alpha_{i,t}+1,\beta_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If agent <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s private decision at time <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">incorrect</span>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,t+1},\beta_{i,t+1})=(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t}+1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,t+1},\beta_{i,t+1})=(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t}+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">These updates reflect the incremental learning of agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s true reliability <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> across different time steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 2</span></span><span id="Thmexample2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmexample2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmexample2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider an agent <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> whose belief about its reliability is modeled by <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}\sim\text{Beta}(2,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}\sim\text{Beta}(2,3)</annotation></semantics></math> and later, after more decisions, by <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}\sim\text{Beta}(20,30)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}\sim\text{Beta}(20,30)</annotation></semantics></math>. The PDFs of these distributions are shown below.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.22413v1/BetaPlot1.png" id="S2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/285;" width="381" height="285" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S2.F2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Beta Belief Visualization.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Thmexample2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmexample2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmexample2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This illustrates how the agent’s internal model assigns probability densities to different possible values of its true reliability <math id="Thmexample2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this example, both pairs of <math id="Thmexample2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> parameters maintain the same proportion, but an increase in the total counts significantly reduces the agent’s uncertainty.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">An Abstention Threshold.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Building on the previous section, agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s confidence <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}=\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,t}&gt;{p_{\text{critical},i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>critical</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}=\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,t}&gt;{p_{\text{critical},i}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}\sim\text{Beta}(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}\sim\text{Beta}(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the agent’s current belief about its true reliability <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> makes a public choice only if its confidence exceeds a specific threshold, denoted as <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that in the voting process, we distinguish <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">private choices</span> and <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">public votes</span>, and that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the total number of decision instances.
At each time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the agent <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">privately</span> decides and learns from feedback; if sufficiently confident, it also <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">publishes</span> a vote.
Let <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,t}\in\{-1,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,t}\in\{-1,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the private decision (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1\equiv\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≡</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1\equiv\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1\equiv{\omega_{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1\equiv{\omega_{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math>). The probability of a decision <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> given a true state <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X_{i,t}=x\mid\Omega_{t}=\omega)=\begin{cases}p_{i}&amp;\text{if }x\text{ encodes }\omega,\\
1-p_{i}&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> encodes </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X_{i,t}=x\mid\Omega_{t}=\omega)=\begin{cases}p_{i}&amp;\text{if }x\text{ encodes }\omega,\\
1-p_{i}&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This means that for agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability of making the correct private choice is always <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. These private choices are used internally by agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to update its belief <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> (and thus <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>) after each decision, regardless of whether it makes a public choice.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that the private decisions of agents are made independently across trials and across agents, defined analogously to the case where we consider one-shot voting instances <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Private Signal Independence)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A collection <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{i,t})_{i\in\{1,\dots,N\},\,t\in\{1,\dots,T\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{i,t})_{i\in\{1,\dots,N\},\,t\in\{1,\dots,T\}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies private signal independence if, for any sequence of ground truths <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}\in\mathcal{W}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}\in\mathcal{W}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{i,t})\in\{-1,1\}^{N\times T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{i,t})\in\{-1,1\}^{N\times T}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\bigwedge_{i=1}^{N}\bigwedge_{t=1}^{T}(X_{i,t}=v_{i,t})\mathrel{\Big|}\bm{\Omega}=\bm{\omega}\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{N}\prod_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{P}\left(X_{i,t}=v_{i,t}\mid\Omega_{t}=\omega_{t}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" mathsize="1.600em">|</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝝎</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\bigwedge_{i=1}^{N}\bigwedge_{t=1}^{T}(X_{i,t}=v_{i,t})\mathrel{\Big|}\bm{\Omega}=\bm{\omega}\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{N}\prod_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{P}\left(X_{i,t}=v_{i,t}\mid\Omega_{t}=\omega_{t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s decision to make a public vote at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is captured by a <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">binary indicator variable</span> <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(t)\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(t)\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }\mathcal{C}_{i,t}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}\\
0&amp;\text{if }\mathcal{C}_{i,t}\leq{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }\mathcal{C}_{i,t}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}\\
0&amp;\text{if }\mathcal{C}_{i,t}\leq{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a deterministic switch at each time step <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>: if agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s confidence <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds the <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math> threshold, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=1</annotation></semantics></math> (indicating a public vote); otherwise, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math> (indicating abstention). Note that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s internal belief state at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s public vote at time step <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}\in\{-1,0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}\in\{-1,0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, is determined by its private choice <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> only if the agent decides to vote publicly. Specifically, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}=X_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}=X_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. That is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}=D_{\text{vote},i}(t)\cdot X_{i,t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}=D_{\text{vote},i}(t)\cdot X_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Given this definition, the overall probability for agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s public vote to align with the true state is:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(V_{i,t}=+1\mid\Omega_{t}=\omega^{*})=\mathbb{P}(D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=1\mid\Omega_{t}=\omega^{*})\,p_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(V_{i,t}=+1\mid\Omega_{t}=\omega^{*})=\mathbb{P}(D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=1\mid\Omega_{t}=\omega^{*})\,p_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">and analogously under <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{t}={\omega_{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{t}={\omega_{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(D_{\text{vote},i}(t)=1)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the probability that agent <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s confidence <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, based on its accumulated experience up to time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, is sufficiently high for it to make a public choice at this time step. Note that in our analysis later, only <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,T}</annotation></semantics></math> enters the final tally; earlier <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>) are specific to the learning period and not aggregated.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The abstention condition, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}\leq\tau_{\text{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}\leq\tau_{\text{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math>, can be expressed explicitly using the properties of the Beta distribution and the regularized incomplete Beta function such that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,t}&gt;{p_{\text{critical},i}})\leq{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>critical</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,t}&gt;{p_{\text{critical},i}})\leq{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-I_{{p_{\text{critical},i}}}(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})\leq{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>critical</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-I_{{p_{\text{critical},i}}}(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})\leq{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p10.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is the regularized incomplete Beta function.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The Regularized Incomplete Beta Function.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The regularized incomplete Beta function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)=\frac{1}{B(\alpha,\beta)}\int_{0}^{x}t^{\alpha-1}(1-t)^{\beta-1}dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)=\frac{1}{B(\alpha,\beta)}\int_{0}^{x}t^{\alpha-1}(1-t)^{\beta-1}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\alpha,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\alpha,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is the complete Beta function:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\alpha,\beta)=\int_{0}^{1}t^{\alpha-1}(1-t)^{\beta-1}dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\alpha,\beta)=\int_{0}^{1}t^{\alpha-1}(1-t)^{\beta-1}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The regularized function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the cumulative distribution function (CDF) of the Beta distribution, such that:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\Psi\leq x)=I_{x}(\alpha,\beta),\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{P}(\Psi&gt;x)=1-I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\Psi\leq x)=I_{x}(\alpha,\beta),\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{P}(\Psi&gt;x)=1-I_{x}(\alpha,\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3</span></span><span id="Thmexample3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmexample3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmexample3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider an agent with <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(4,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(4,3)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{critical},i}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{critical},i}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. Its confidence is</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}=\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,t}&gt;0.5)=1-I_{0.5}(4,3)\approx 0.65." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.65</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}=\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,t}&gt;0.5)=1-I_{0.5}(4,3)\approx 0.65.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmexample3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmexample3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus the agent assigns a <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="65\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>65</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">65\%</annotation></semantics></math> probability that its true reliability exceeds <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. If the abstention target is <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> it would publish; if <math id="Thmexample3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}=0.75</annotation></semantics></math> it would abstain.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Framework Summary.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The process unfolds over <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> discrete steps involving a sequence of independent tasks. Rounds <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,\dots,T-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,\dots,T-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> constitute the <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">calibration phase</span>, where agents learn about their own capabilities; round <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">decision phase</span>, where public votes on the final task <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are aggregated.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Model Assumption (Static Competence vs. Dynamic Belief):</span> We assume each agent’s true reliability <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed (representing inherent capability). The “learning” process acts as a <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">confidence calibration phase</span>: agents do not improve their task performance <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> over time, but rather refine their <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">estimate</span> of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to distinguish whether they are sufficiently reliable to vote.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Within each round <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>, the protocol proceeds as follows:
(i) <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Belief State:</span> The pre-decision belief <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,t},\beta_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math> summarizes feedback from tasks <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math>, inducing a confidence score <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>;
(ii) <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gating:</span> The agent chooses to <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">publish or abstain</span> based on its internal estimate: <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(t)=\mathbf{1}\{\mathcal{C}_{i,t}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(t)=\mathbf{1}\{\mathcal{C}_{i,t}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>;
(iii) <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Task Execution:</span> A new task <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn. The private signal <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,t}\in\{-1,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,t}\in\{-1,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is realized according to the agent’s fixed competence <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (Bernoulli trial), independent of the current belief state;
(iv) <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Feedback:</span> The public vote is <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}=D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(t)\cdot X_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}=D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(t)\cdot X_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Correctness feedback on <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is observed (regardless of abstention), updating the belief to <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,t+1},\beta_{i,t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,t+1},\beta_{i,t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Only the published votes <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,T}</annotation></semantics></math> at the final step are aggregated for the collective decision.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Probabilistic Modeling of Dynamic Beliefs and Collective Voting</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section lays the theoretical groundwork for an analysis of the final majority vote outcome, specifically bounding the probability of the correct alternative winning. This analysis integrates the dynamic evolution of agent beliefs and their abstention probabilities. Our approach proceeds in three key steps: We first introduce a probabilistic model that captures the cumulative information growth of agents across trials, formalizing this with <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">martingales</span> and <span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">filtrations</span>. Subsequently, we derive the expected value of the aggregated votes favoring the correct alternative at the final time step. Finally, to facilitate the application of the <span id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Azuma-Hoeffding inequality</span>, a concentration inequality designed to provide tight bounds on the probability that a sum of dependent random variables deviates significantly from its mean, we construct a martingale difference sequence based on <span id="S3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Doob martingales</span>. This sequence effectively isolates and quantifies the total deviation of the final vote, which is precisely what the Azuma-Hoeffding inequality operates on.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Martingales and Filtration.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To rigorously analyze the behavior of our agents and derive results akin to a jury theorem for their collective decisions, we establish a robust probabilistic framework. This framework, based on the concepts of <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">martingales</span> and <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">filtrations</span>, allows us to model the dynamic evolution of agents’ beliefs and the accumulation of information within the system. We mostly follow the definitions given in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, adapted to our framework.
<span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Martingales</span> and <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">filtrations</span> have clear intuitive meanings in thinking about betting games. For example, <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">martingales</span> can be thought of as the fortune of a player betting on a fair game <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, formally described as a special kind of sequence of random variables whose values evolve over time. A <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">filtration</span> can be thought of as sets of information increasing as the martingales evolve, capturing the game’s history. Roughly speaking, in our setting, we can see the sequence of decisions made by the agents, as well as the feedback they receive in order to update their beliefs, as such a game.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to formally introduce both concepts we need to define <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">probability space</span> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-algebra</span> first:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A probability space is a triple <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{S},\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{S},\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is a set of outcomes, <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is a collection of events (subsets of <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}:\mathcal{F}\rightarrow[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}:\mathcal{F}\rightarrow[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability measure. We assume that <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra, meaning it is a nonempty collection of subsets of <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then its complement </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{c}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{c}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a countable sequence of sets, then </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{j=1}^{\infty}A_{j}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{j=1}^{\infty}A_{j}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These properties ensure that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> comprises all subsets of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> for which we can meaningfully assign probabilities. We first introduce <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">filtration</span> and <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">martingales</span> with respect to a single agent, extending these concepts to the multi-agent case shortly after.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Filtration)<span id="Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A filtration is a sequence of increasing <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebras <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t=0,1,\dots,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t=0,1,\dots,T}</annotation></semantics></math> on a probability space <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{S},\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{S},\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, a filtration has the property <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{s}\subseteq\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{s}\subseteq\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math> which signifies that information (or events that are observable) only grows over time. In our context, considering a single agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{i,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{i,0}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s prior belief about its reliability derived from <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> captures all private outcomes observed by agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> up to trial <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, which are used to update agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s belief <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>. From this, we can define an <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">adapted stochastic process</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Adapted Stochastic Process)<span id="Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A stochastic process <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{t})_{t=0,1,\dots,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{t})_{t=0,1,\dots,T}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. a sequence of random variables, is said to be adapted to a filtration <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t=0,1,\dots,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t=0,1,\dots,T}</annotation></semantics></math> if, for each <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable with respect to <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This means that the value of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is known given the information available at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. Having defined filtrations as well as stochastic processes being adapted to filtrations, we can introduce <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">martingales</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Martingale)<span id="Thmdefinition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A stochastic process, denoted</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmdefinition5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{t})_{t=0,1,\dots,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{t})_{t=0,1,\dots,T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmdefinition5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, is called a martingale with respect to a filtration <math id="Thmdefinition5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> if it satisfies the following three conditions:</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|M_{t}|]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|M_{t}|]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. (Integrability: the expected absolute value of the process at any time is finite.)</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is adapted to </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. (Adaptedness: the value of </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is known given the information up to time </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.)</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[M_{t+1}\mid\mathcal{F}_{t}]=M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[M_{t+1}\mid\mathcal{F}_{t}]=M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. (Fair Game Property: the expected future value of the process, given all past and present information, is equal to its current value.)</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, a martingale is your running best estimate of a <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">target random variable</span> as information accumulates: conditioned on what you currently know, your expected next estimate equals the estimate you hold now. This is exactly the idea we use when we form the Doob martingale to apply the Azuma–Hoeffding inequality.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multiple Agents.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We extend our model to <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> agents, each facing the binary decision problem <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> times. Each agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math>) has its own true reliability <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial Beta parameters <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})</annotation></semantics></math>, critical probability <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\text{critical},i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mtext>critical</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\text{critical},i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and abstention threshold <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When dealing with multiple agents, the definition of the filtration needs to encompass the information available to all agents. Assuming agents do not observe each other’s private outcomes or confidence states, the natural filtration for the collective system would be the <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">joint filtration</span> generated by the private outcomes of all agents representing the combined history of all private outcomes observed by all agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This can be captured by an event-based filtration, i.e. the sequential revelation of each individual private signal across all agents and time steps.
We define <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=NT" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=NT</annotation></semantics></math> as the total number of private outcomes revealed over all agents and all time steps. That is, we order the <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\times T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\times T</annotation></semantics></math> individual agent-time-step private outcomes sequentially using a combined index <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=(t-1)N+i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=(t-1)N+i</annotation></semantics></math>, running from <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="NT" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NT</annotation></semantics></math>. Let these outcomes be ordered <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(1)},X_{(2)},\dots,X_{(K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(1)},X_{(2)},\dots,X_{(K)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the ordering progresses through time steps first, then through agents (e.g., <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(1)}=X_{1,1},\dots,X_{(N)}=X_{N,1},X_{(N+1)}=X_{1,2},\dots,X_{(NT)}=X_{N,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(1)}=X_{1,1},\dots,X_{(N)}=X_{N,1},X_{(N+1)}=X_{1,2},\dots,X_{(NT)}=X_{N,T}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The event-based filtration <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})_{k=0,1,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})_{k=0,1,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of increasing <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebras, where <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the collective information generated by the first <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> individual private outcomes revealed across the system.
Formally, for each <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\dots,NT\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\dots,NT\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}=\sigma(\{X_{(j)}:j\in\{1,\dots,k\}\})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}=\sigma(\{X_{(j)}:j\in\{1,\dots,k\}\})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra representing initial knowledge.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is this event-based filtration <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> that serves as the basis for constructing the Doob martingale in the context of concentration inequalities on the aggregate vote, as it accounts for the impact of each single new piece of information. Observe that the filtration <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is an analyst filtration; individual agents observe only their own histories (<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{i,t}\ :=\ \sigma\!\big(\{X_{i,s}:1\leq s\leq t\}\big),\textit{for \&gt;}t=0,1,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{i,t}\ :=\ \sigma\!\big(\{X_{i,s}:1\leq s\leq t\}\big),\textit{for \&gt;}t=0,1,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math>), but not those of other agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now that we have a probabilistic model for the internal belief updating process of multiple agents based on their private decisions, we proceed to model the public votes in a next step.
Recall that we defined the random variable representing agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s net public vote at time step <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows: <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, if agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> publicly votes for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>, if agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> publicly votes for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\omega_{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\omega_{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, if agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> abstains.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Following the notation of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeauthor"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karge et al.</a></cite> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeyear"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">2024</a></cite>), the collective net public vote at the final time step <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> s.t. <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> wins the collective vote iff <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}V_{i,T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}V_{i,T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Expected Collective Net Public Vote at Final Time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this subsection, we analyze the vote on the final task <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. We condition on the target true state being <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\cdot):=\mathbb{P}(\cdot\mid\Omega_{T}=\omega^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\cdot):=\mathbb{P}(\cdot\mid\Omega_{T}=\omega^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To characterize the collective vote at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, we first determine its expectation. By linearity of expectation, the <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">expected collective net public vote at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></span> is the sum of the expected individual net public votes at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}V_{i,T}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}V_{i,T}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For each agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected individual net public vote at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[V_{i,T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[V_{i,T}]</annotation></semantics></math>, is derived as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)\cdot X_{i,T}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)\cdot X_{i,T}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> depends on agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s updated belief state at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (determined by their private history up to <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{i,T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{i,T-1}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable), and by conditional independence given that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,T}</annotation></semantics></math> is agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s private choice at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, we can apply the law of total expectation:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}\!\big[\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)X_{i,T}\mid\mathcal{F}_{i,T-1}]\,\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}\!\big[\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)X_{i,T}\mid\mathcal{F}_{i,T-1}]\,\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}\!\big[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[X_{i,T}\mid\mathcal{F}_{i,T-1}]\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}\!\big[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[X_{i,T}\mid\mathcal{F}_{i,T-1}]\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)\cdot(2p_{i}-1)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)\cdot(2p_{i}-1)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant (true reliability), the term <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2p_{i}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2p_{i}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> is also a constant. Therefore, we can factor it out of the expectation:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]=(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]=(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The expected value of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability that agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> decides to vote publicly at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]=\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]=\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting this back into the sum for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">To compute <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}})</annotation></semantics></math> for each agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must sum over all possible numbers of correct outcomes (<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>) that could have occurred in the <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math> preceding trials <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for that specific agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></span>. If <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> outcomes were correct and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T-1-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T-1-k)</annotation></semantics></math> were incorrect, then agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s Beta parameters at time <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> would be <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,T}=\alpha_{i,0}+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,T}=\alpha_{i,0}+k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,T}=\beta_{i,0}+(T-1-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,T}=\beta_{i,0}+(T-1-k)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,0}</annotation></semantics></math> are agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s initial prior parameters for its own competence <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The probability of observing <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> correct outcomes in <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math> trials, given agent <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s true reliability <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, follows a binomial distribution:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}})=\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\mathbf{1}\Big\{1-I_{{p_{\text{critical},i}}}\big(\alpha_{i,0}+k,\beta_{i,0}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">abstain</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">I</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">critical</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}})=\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\mathbf{1}\Big\{1-I_{{p_{\text{critical},i}}}\big(\alpha_{i,0}+k,\beta_{i,0}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(T-1-k)\big)&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}\Big\}\cdot\binom{T-1}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{T-1-k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">abstain</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(T-1-k)\big)&gt;{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}\Big\}\cdot\binom{T-1}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{T-1-k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟏</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is an indicator function, which equals 1 if the condition is true and 0 otherwise, i.e. we select only those histories (i.e., values of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>) for which the agent’s confidence exceeds the abstention threshold, contributing to the total probability of voting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Martingale Difference Sequence.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To bound the probability that the correct alternative wins the majority vote across all agents at the final time step <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, we analyze the deviation of the total aggregated net public vote from its expected value.
For this purpose, we construct a <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Doob martingale</span>. This construction directly yields a sequence of random variables whose sum represents the total deviation, and whose individual increments (<span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">martingale differences</span>) have a zero conditional expectation. To formally define this martingale, which is conditioned on the accumulating information in the system, we first need to establish a comprehensive filtration for the entire collective.
Recall that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the event-based filtration capturing information from the first <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> observed private outcomes, which orders all individual private outcomes observed by agents across all trials and which will serve as the underlying filtration.
We define a <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Doob martingale</span> <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{k})_{k=0,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{k})_{k=0,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and the filtration <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Doob Martingale <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmdefinition7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This martingale has the following properties:</p>
<ul id="S3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the initial step (<math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{0}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{0}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> contains no information about the random outcomes).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the final step (<math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=NT" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=NT</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{NT}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{NT}]=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{NT}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{NT}]=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> (since all private outcomes up to time <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> for all agents are observed, <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is fully determined).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze the deviation from the mean, we consider a related martingale, i.e. the centered variant of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> be the centered random variable representing the total deviation of interest. This centering is crucial because the Azuma-Hoeffding inequality operates on a sequence of martingale differences that have a zero conditional mean, a property that follows naturally from the centered martingale:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This new martingale <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> directly represents our best estimate of the total deviation, given all the private outcomes revealed up to step <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
Notice that:</p>
<ul id="S3.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the initial step (<math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{0}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{0}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{0}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{0}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the final step (<math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=NT" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=NT</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{NT}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{NT}]=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{NT}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{NT}]=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The total deviation of interest, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math>, can then be expressed as the sum of the <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">martingale differences</span> of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is a direct application of the telescoping sum property, where the sum of successive differences of a sequence simplifies to the difference between its final and initial terms:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=M^{\prime}_{NT}-M^{\prime}_{0}=\sum_{k=1}^{NT}(M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=M^{\prime}_{NT}-M^{\prime}_{0}=\sum_{k=1}^{NT}(M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In the next section, we will apply a concentration inequality known as the <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Azuma-Hoeffding inequality</span> to derive a lower bound on <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> winning the majority vote. This requires the sequence <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, to form a <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">martingale difference sequence</span>. This means it must satisfy the following properties <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Integrability:</span> <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[|D_{k}|]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[|D_{k}|]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Adaptedness:</span> <math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable with respect to <math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Zero Conditional Mean:</span> <math id="S3.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Observe that the zero conditional mean property is directly linked to the fair game property: if the expected future value of a martingale (given all past and present information) equals its current value, then the expected change in that martingale must necessarily be zero.
To prepare the Azuma-Hoeffding derivation, we show that:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> forms a martingale difference sequence with respect to the filtration <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof Sketch.</span>
Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z:=V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z:=V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}]</annotation></semantics></math> and define the Doob martingale
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}:=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}:=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math> with differences <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}:=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}:=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
(i) <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Integrability:</em> <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}\in[-N,N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}\in[-N,N]</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded, so
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[|D_{k}|]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[|D_{k}|]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
(ii) <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Adaptedness:</em> <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>–measurable by definition of conditional
expectation; <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>–measurable and therefore <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>–measurable
since <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is a filtration; thus <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>–measurable.
(iii) <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Zero conditional mean:</em> By the tower property,
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-M^{\prime}_{k-1}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-M^{\prime}_{k-1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-M^{\prime}_{k-1}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-M^{\prime}_{k-1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{k})_{k=1}^{NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{k})_{k=1}^{NT}</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale difference sequence w.r.t. <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The full proof can be found in subsection <a href="#Sx1.SS1" title="5.1 Proof for Proposition 1. ‣ Appendix ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> of the appendix.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To find good tail estimates for the probability of <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> winning the majority vote at the final time step, we utilize the one-sided variant of the Azuma-Hoeffding inequality. More specifically, the objective is to derive a lower bound for the probability <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Azuma-Hoeffding inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a sequence of random variables <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{k})_{k=1,\dots,K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{k})_{k=1,\dots,K}</annotation></semantics></math> that forms a martingale difference sequence with respect to a filtration <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{k}|\leq c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{k}|\leq c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\sum_{k=1}^{K}Z_{k}\leq-\epsilon\right)\leq e^{-\frac{\epsilon^{2}}{2\sum_{k=1}^{K}c_{k}^{2}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\sum_{k=1}^{K}Z_{k}\leq-\epsilon\right)\leq e^{-\frac{\epsilon^{2}}{2\sum_{k=1}^{K}c_{k}^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The sequence <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math> forms such a martingale difference sequence with respect to the filtration <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we established in Proposition 1.
A central concern when applying the inequality is to show that the martingale difference sequence is, in fact, bounded. This we show in the following lemma:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the martingale differences with respect to the event-based filtration <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})_{k=0,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})_{k=0,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\dots,NT\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\dots,NT\}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a bound <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|\leq c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|\leq c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, if <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to agent <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=|2p_{i}-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=|2p_{i}-1|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, the sum of the squares of these bounds across all agents and time steps is:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof Sketch.</span>
Let <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}:=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}:=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z:=V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z:=V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}]</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}:=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}:=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math>
when the revealed outcome is <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}=X_{i^{*},t^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}=X_{i^{*},t^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}=D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\,X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}=D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\,X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}\in\{-1,+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}\in\{-1,+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>; by conditional
independence, <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[X_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{\cdot}]=2p_{i^{*}}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⋅</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[X_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{\cdot}]=2p_{i^{*}}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\big(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\big(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]\big),</annotation></semantics></math>
a difference of two probabilities, so <math id="S4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|\leq|2p_{i^{*}}-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|\leq|2p_{i^{*}}-1|</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=T</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=V_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=V_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)(2p_{i^{*}}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)(2p_{i^{*}}-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, giving
<math id="S4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\,(X_{i^{*},T}-(2p_{i^{*}}-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)\,(X_{i^{*},T}-(2p_{i^{*}}-1))</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Summing squares over all events yields
<math id="S4.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The full proof can be found in subsection <a href="#Sx1.SS2" title="5.2 Proof for Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> of the appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, each increment is the one-step change in our running forecast
when a single private outcome is revealed.
If the revealed outcome belongs to an earlier learning round (<math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>), it cannot change the final private vote <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math>; it only shifts the <span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">publish probability</span> for agent <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{vote},i^{*}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the revealed outcome is the final one (<math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=T</annotation></semantics></math>), it collapses the remaining uncertainty about <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}\in\{-1,0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}\in\{-1,0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, moving a conditional mean by at most <math id="S4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. From this, we can derive our main theorem:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a majority voting setting for <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> agents over a learning period over <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math> rounds, and a final voting round <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> for agents with individual competence values <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, prior pseudo–counts <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})</annotation></semantics></math> for a Beta belief about its own reliability <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
a critical competence level <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{critical},i}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{critical},i}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> it aims to exceed, and an abstention threshold <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>: the minimum posterior probability of exceeding <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{critical},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{critical},i}</annotation></semantics></math> required to vote publicly. We assume private signals are conditionally independent across agents and time given the sequence of ground truths <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> (Def. <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Private Signal Independence). ‣ An Abstention Threshold. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
Then it is guaranteed that the success probability of the
majority vote is at least</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-e^{\left(-\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]\right)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-e^{\left(-\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]\right)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
From Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Azuma-Hoeffding inequality []). ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we obtain:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}\leq 0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}\leq 0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}\left({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\leq-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}\left({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\leq-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S4.Ex36.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">We apply the Azuma-Hoeffding inequality with <math id="S4.Ex36.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S4.Ex37.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}=D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">Z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">D</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}=D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.Ex37.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, and <math id="S4.Ex37.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-e^{\left(-\frac{(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}])^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-e^{\left(-\frac{(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}])^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S4.Ex39.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">Substitute the expected total net public vote (derived previously):</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"> <span id="S4.Ex40.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="S4.Ex40.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔼</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔼</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">V</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔼</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">D</mi><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">vote</mtext><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i,T}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)].</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-e^{\left(-\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]\right)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-e^{\left(-\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]\right)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This derived bound quantifies the minimum probability of winning the majority vote at the final time step. We briefly recall that <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the probability of an agent to vote publicly, can be computed from the model parameters alone, as outlined in Equation <a href="#S3.Ex27" title="In Expected Collective Net Public Vote at Final Time 𝑇. ‣ 3 Probabilistic Modeling of Dynamic Beliefs and Collective Voting ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, by summing over all possible learning histories, each weighted by its binomial probability.
Recall that we see <em id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hallucination</em> as a false positive: accepting an <em id="S4.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">invalid</em> item <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>. Applying the same Azuma–Hoeffding derivation under <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}={\omega_{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}={\omega_{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math> (see subsection <a href="#Sx1.SS3" title="5.3 Proof for the Hallucination Bound. ‣ Appendix ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> in the appendix for the full proof), we obtain an upper bound on collective hallucination:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Collective Hallucination Bound)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{{\omega_{\dagger}}}\!\big(V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}&gt;0\big)\ \leq\ e^{\!\left(-\frac{\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\,\mathbb{E}_{{\omega_{\dagger}}}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]\Big)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℙ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.460em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.738em">≤</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="3.200em" minsize="3.200em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.450em" minsize="0.450em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">vote</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="3.200em" minsize="3.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.450em" minsize="0.450em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.400em" minsize="2.400em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="2.400em" minsize="2.400em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{{\omega_{\dagger}}}\!\big(V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}&gt;0\big)\ \leq\ e^{\!\left(-\frac{\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\,\mathbb{E}_{{\omega_{\dagger}}}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]\Big)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Equation <a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> not only allows us to assess the success probability of multiple agents in practice, but also lets us derive the classical Condorcet conclusion: the probability that majority voting selects the correct alternative converges to <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> as the number of agents grows. Our convergence result relies on two assumptions. First, the average competence must stay bounded away from <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}\geq 0.5+\Delta p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}\geq 0.5+\Delta p</annotation></semantics></math>). Second, we assume that the gate does not become arbitrarily strict for new agents. That is, for every competent agent in the sequence, there is a lower-bounded probability of publishing. We refer to this as a <span id="S4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">uniformly nondegenerate gate</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n:=T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n:=T-1</annotation></semantics></math>. For agent <math id="S4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of correct private outcomes across the <math id="S4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> learning trials.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 8</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniformly Nondegenerate Gate)<span id="Thmdefinition8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=T-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}(p):=\mathbb{P}(\text{Agent }i\text{ publishes}\mid\text{competence }p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Agent </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> publishes</mtext></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">competence </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}(p):=\mathbb{P}(\text{Agent }i\text{ publishes}\mid\text{competence }p)</annotation></semantics></math>. The gate is uniformly nondegenerate if there exists a constant <math id="Thmdefinition8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\min}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\min}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all agents <math id="Thmdefinition8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Thmdefinition8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0.5</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}(p)\geq q_{\min}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}(p)\geq q_{\min}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a sequence of agents in the majority voting setting of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Fix the horizon <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that for the sequence of agents:
(1) The average competence satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\geq 0.5+\Delta p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\geq 0.5+\Delta p</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; and
(2) The gate is uniformly nondegenerate.
Then, the probability of the electorate to identify the correct alternative in the final voting round <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> converges to 1 as <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof Sketch.</span>
We proceed in <span id="S4.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">four</span> steps:
(i) Under the distribution-level reliability model, the number of learning successes <math id="S4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a Binomial distribution;
(ii) We show that the posterior confidence is strictly non-decreasing in <math id="S4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, implying the publish rule is a <span id="S4.p9.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">success-count threshold</span> (<math id="S4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}\geq k_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}\geq k_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>);
(iii) Using the uniform non-degeneracy and average competence assumptions, we lower-bound the expected vote margin;
(iv) Substituting this margin into the Azuma-Hoeffding bound yields an error term that decays exponentially with <math id="S4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.
The full proof is in: Appendix <a href="#Sx1.SS4" title="5.4 Proof for Theorem 3. ‣ Appendix ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.22413v1/PlotCont4.png" id="S4.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/347;" width="476" height="347" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="S4.F3.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=20,\bar{p}=0.55,{{p_{\text{critical},i}}=0.5},{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}=0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">20</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.55</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">critical</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.5</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">abstain</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=20,\bar{p}=0.55,{{p_{\text{critical},i}}=0.5},{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}=0.5}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.F3.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.22413v1/PlotCont2.png" id="S4.F3.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/347;" width="476" height="347" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="S4.F3.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=20,\bar{p}=0.55,{{p_{\text{critical},i}}=0.5},N=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">20</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.55</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">critical</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.5</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">50</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=20,\bar{p}=0.55,{{p_{\text{critical},i}}=0.5},N=50</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.F3.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Empirical Simulation and Equation <a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> visualization under two configurations.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Empirical Simulations</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we empirically assess the bound from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> by Monte Carlo simulation of the full process, and compare this to the Azuma–Hoeffding lower bound (Equation <a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) computed from the same parameters. For a pseudocode description of the implementation, we refer the reader to subsection <a href="#Sx1.SS5" title="5.5 Pseudocode for Empirical Evaluation. ‣ Appendix ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a> of the appendix.
In each simulation round we: (i) draw all private outcomes for all agents over the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\!-\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!-\!1</annotation></semantics></math> learning tasks; (ii) update each agent’s Beta counts; (iii) apply the gate at time <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{critical},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{critical},i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math>; (iv) sample each publishing agent’s final private vote on <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>; and (v) record whether the final majority is correct. Repeating this <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math> times yields the empirical success probability (the share of rounds in which the correct alternative wins).
We consider four agent pools, accounting for different competence distributions, and their interaction with the abstention gate, across two parameter configurations. That is, (i) Homogeneous agents (identical competencies); (ii) Heterogeneous agents with a prescribed <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mtext>abstain</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\tau_{\text{abstain},i}}</annotation></semantics></math>-value, and uniform Beta priors (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})=(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})=(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>); (iii) Heterogeneous agents that never abstain (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>abstain</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>) as a baseline comparison; (iv) Heterogeneous agents with priors chosen contrary to their true reliability.
That is, setting (iv) studies miscalibrated Beta priors, implemented as follows: For agent <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with true reliability <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose a prior strength <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (total pseudo–count) and set (for <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for numerical stability):
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,0}\ :=\ \max\!\big(\kappa(1-p_{i}),\,\varepsilon\big),\beta_{i,0}\ :=\ \max\!\big(\kappa p_{i},\,\varepsilon\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,0}\ :=\ \max\!\big(\kappa(1-p_{i}),\,\varepsilon\big),\beta_{i,0}\ :=\ \max\!\big(\kappa p_{i},\,\varepsilon\big).</annotation></semantics></math> That is, competent agents (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}&gt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}&gt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) start <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">pessimistic</span>, and incompetent agents (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) start <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">optimistic</span>. For all settings, we assume an average reliability of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}=0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}=0.55</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=20</annotation></semantics></math> trials, and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{critical},i}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{critical},i}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. Heterogeneity is implemented by assigning <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\in\{0.35,\,0.75\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.35</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 0.75</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\in\{0.35,\,0.75\}</annotation></semantics></math> to equal-sized halves, so that <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}=0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}=0.55</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#S4.F3.sf1" title="Figure 3(a) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a>, we plot the bound and empirical success probability as the number of agents (<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>) varies, prescribing <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for all agents. In Figure <a href="#S4.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3(b) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a>, we plot against a common <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>abstain</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=50</annotation></semantics></math> agents.
Across both settings, the gated models (blue: heterogeneous with uniform priors; red: heterogeneous with contrary priors) dominate the non-abstaining baseline (orange) and the homogeneous pool (green): selective abstention suppresses low-competence voters, so the publishing electorate is, in expectation, stronger, leading to both a higher empirical success rate, and theoretical minimum success probability. An exception appears in Fig. <a href="#S4.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3(b) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a> for very large gates: once <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>abstain</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds what even the better half (<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>) can typically certify, many agents stop publishing and performance degrades, while the non-abstaining baseline remains roughly flat.
In both plots, the empirical success rates (dashed) lie well above the theoretical curves (solid). This is expected as <a href="#S4.E2" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is a <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">worst-case</span> concentration bound, protecting against the most unfavorable realizations by only using coarse information about the process.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Summary and Future Work</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we introduced a probabilistic framework to analyze collective decision-making with endogenous participation. By employing martingales and filtrations, we captured the dynamic evolution of agents’ confidence and their resulting decision to vote or abstain. Our primary contribution is the derivation of a non-asymptotic lower bound on the probability of a correct majority, alongside an asymptotic guarantee that extends the classical CJT to settings with heterogeneous agents and confidence-based abstention.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This framework offers a theoretical bridge between two distinct views on abstention: the <span id="S5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">strategic</span> view of social choice theory (where agents abstain to avoid pivoting the vote incorrectly) and the <span id="S5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">epistemic</span> view of statistical learning (where agents abstain due to low confidence). We showed that “calibrated” agents who simply maximize their own precision naturally improve the collective information state.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For future work, we plan to explore three avenues. First, from a theoretical standpoint, we aim to derive tighter concentration bounds by incorporating the variance structure of the martingale difference sequence (e.g., using <span id="S5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Freedman’s inequality</span>). Second, regarding social choice axioms, we wish to relax the independence assumption to model correlated information sources, a common scenario in committee deliberations. Finally, we plan to apply this framework to the design of hybrid intelligence systems, using Large Language Models (LLMs) as calibrated agents to empirically validate how confidence-gated voting mitigates group-level hallucination in collective decision-making. This will involve: (i) instantiating the agents as individual LLMs or as different reasoning paths of a single LLM, (ii) using a feedback loop to simulate the learning process and update their competence beliefs, and (iii) evaluating the success of our confidence-based abstention mechanism in mitigating hallucinations on a range of binary decision tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix</h2>

<section id="Sx1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Proof for Proposition 1.</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We verify that <math id="Sx1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a martingale difference sequence with respect to the filtration <math id="Sx1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that we let</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">be the centered random variable representing the total deviation of interest and that we can then construct a Doob martingale for this centered variable:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Each <math id="Sx1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the change in the conditional expectation of the centered sum of final votes <math id="Sx1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> when the <math id="Sx1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th private outcome is revealed.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We show each property individually.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">1. <span id="Sx1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Integrability (<math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[|D_{k}|]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[|D_{k}|]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>:
By the triangle inequality, <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|=|M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}|\leq|M^{\prime}_{k}|+|M^{\prime}_{k-1}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|=|M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}|\leq|M^{\prime}_{k}|+|M^{\prime}_{k-1}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The random variable <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum of <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> terms (agents’ votes at time <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>), each bounded within <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{-1,0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{-1,0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded within <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-N,N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-N,N]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, the centered variable <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> is also bounded. Specifically, its values lie within <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-N-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}],N-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-N-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}],N-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> is itself bounded within <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-N,N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-N,N]</annotation></semantics></math>, the range of the centered variable is at most <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-2N,2N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-2N,2N]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The conditional expectations <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> are therefore also bounded random variables. A bounded random variable has a finite expected absolute value. Consequently, <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[|D_{k}|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[|D_{k}|]</annotation></semantics></math> is finite.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">2. <span id="Sx1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Adaptedness (<math id="Sx1.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable with respect to <math id="Sx1.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">A random variable <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable if, for every Borel set <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> in the measurable space <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R},\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R},\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R})</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the collection of all subsets of <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfy the properties of a <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra (containing the empty set and <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and being closed under complementation and countable unions), and thus are precisely the sets to which a probability measure can be consistently assigned, the preimage <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{-1}(B)=\{s\in\mathsf{S}\mid X(s)\in B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖲</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{-1}(B)=\{s\in\mathsf{S}\mid X(s)\in B\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an element of the <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.
In essence, this means that for any possible value or range of values that <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> can take, we can determine, solely by observing the events in <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, whether <math id="Sx1.SS1.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> falls into that value or range.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">In our specific context, the random variables <math id="Sx1.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (and thus <math id="Sx1.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>) take on values that are conditional expectations of the centered variable <math id="Sx1.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math>. A key property of conditional expectation is that <math id="Sx1.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{H}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{H}]</annotation></semantics></math> is always <math id="Sx1.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable for any random variable <math id="Sx1.SS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> for which the expectation exists <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s demonstrate why <math id="Sx1.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Sx1.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable. For <math id="Sx1.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="Sx1.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable, both <math id="Sx1.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> must be <math id="Sx1.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Sx1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Measurability of <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span>
By the very definition of a Doob martingale, <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math> is, by construction, <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable. Therefore, for any Borel set <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R})</annotation></semantics></math>, the event <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s\in\mathsf{S}\mid M^{\prime}_{k}(s)\in B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖲</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s\in\mathsf{S}\mid M^{\prime}_{k}(s)\in B\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an element of <math id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Measurability of <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span>
The random variable <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> is, by definition, <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable. Since <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})_{k=0,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})_{k=0,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math> is a filtration, it satisfies the property that <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that any random variable that is measurable with respect to the smaller <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is also measurable with respect to the larger <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the case since for every Borel set <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that if <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{-1}(B)\in\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{-1}(B)\in\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{-1}(B)\in\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{-1}(B)\in\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Since both <math id="Sx1.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="Sx1.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable random variables, their difference, <math id="Sx1.SS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, is also <math id="Sx1.SS1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable. This follows from the fact that for any two measurable functions, their difference is also measurable <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>.
This confirms that the sequence <math id="Sx1.SS1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{k})_{k=1,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math> is adapted to the filtration <math id="Sx1.SS1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})_{k=0,\dots,NT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})_{k=0,\dots,NT}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">3. <span id="Sx1.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Zero Conditional Mean</span> (<math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>):
We expand <math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Sx1.Ex46.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">(By linearity of conditional expectation)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k-1}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k-1}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p14.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable with respect to <math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., known given <math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k-1}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k-1}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the first term, by the tower property of conditional expectation (<math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> for any random variable <math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> given that the filtration is ordered sequentially):</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[M^{\prime}_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p14.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting these back, we find:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=M^{\prime}_{k-1}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{k}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]=M^{\prime}_{k-1}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p14.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, all three conditions are satisfied, confirming that <math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed a martingale difference sequence with respect to <math id="Sx1.SS1.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Proof for Lemma 2.</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that we let</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">be the centered random variable representing the total deviation of interest and that we can then construct a Doob martingale for this centered variable:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Z\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Each <math id="Sx1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=M^{\prime}_{k}-M^{\prime}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the change in the conditional expectation of the centered sum of final votes <math id="Sx1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> when the <math id="Sx1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th private outcome is revealed.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">As a general strategy to determine <math id="Sx1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Sx1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math>, we determine the maximal change in expectation we can obtain from a single martingale difference. More specifically, we consider a specific but arbitrarily chosen event <math id="Sx1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> in the event-based filtration and take into account the time of its occurrence.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Sx1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{*},t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{*},t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the specific agent and time step corresponding to the <math id="Sx1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th private outcome, <math id="Sx1.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}=X_{i^{*},t^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}=X_{i^{*},t^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The filtration <math id="Sx1.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> contains all information in <math id="Sx1.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> plus the outcome of <math id="Sx1.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The variable <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditional expectation of <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{N}(V_{j,T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{j,T}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{N}(V_{j,T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{j,T}])</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}=X_{i^{*},t^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}=X_{i^{*},t^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is revealed, it only affects the conditional expectation of <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> (and consequently the term <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]</annotation></semantics></math>). The conditional expectations of other agents’ votes <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{j,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{j,T}</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) are independent of <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and thus their contribution to the change is zero.
Thus, the martingale difference <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> simplifies to:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant, i.e. an unconditional expectation (which we can denote as <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}]</annotation></semantics></math>), and recalling the linearity property of conditional expectation (<math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[A-B\mid\mathcal{F}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[A\mid\mathcal{F}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[B\mid\mathcal{F}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[A-B\mid\mathcal{F}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[A\mid\mathcal{F}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[B\mid\mathcal{F}]</annotation></semantics></math>) and that the conditional expectation of a constant is the constant itself (<math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mu\mid\mathcal{F}]=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mu\mid\mathcal{F}]=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>), we can expand the terms:</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}-\mu\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}-\mu\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}-\mu\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}-\mu\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mu\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mu\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\left(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mu\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\left(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mu\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mu\right)-\left(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-\mu\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mu\right)-\left(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]-\mu\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mu-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]+\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mu-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]+\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p">The individual net public vote <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> for agent <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded within <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{-1,0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{-1,0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, any conditional expectation of <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> must also lie within the range <math id="Sx1.SS2.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We now establish the bounds <math id="Sx1.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Sx1.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math> based on the time step <math id="Sx1.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of the revealed outcome <math id="Sx1.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="Sx1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">If <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to agent <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>:</span>
In this case, <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}=X_{i^{*},t^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}=X_{i^{*},t^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a private choice made by agent <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> at a time step prior to the final vote.
We have <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The term <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> represents agent <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>’s private choice at time <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. By our distribution-level reliability assumption, private choices are independent across trials.
This means <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of all past private outcomes (including <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},t^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},t^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the entire filtration <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> (which is determined by prior information), since the distribution of <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> (here <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}=\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}=\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) and not on past history. Therefore, we can write:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.I2.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[X_{i^{*},T}\mid D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T),\mathcal{H}_{k}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[X_{i^{*},T}\mid D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T),\mathcal{H}_{k}]\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"> <span id="Sx1.Ex64.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">Since <math id="Sx1.Ex64.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of all past outcomes</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"> <span id="Sx1.Ex65.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">which determine <math id="Sx1.Ex65.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.Ex65.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, the inner expectation simplifies to:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"> <span id="Sx1.Ex67.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">Then, as <math id="Sx1.Ex67.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2p_{i^{*}}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2p_{i^{*}}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant, it can be factored out of the outer expectation.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we made use of the <span id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Tower Property of Conditional Expectation</span>. This property states that for any random variable <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> and nested <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebras <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{1}\subseteq\mathcal{G}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{1}\subseteq\mathcal{G}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{G}_{1}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{G}_{2}]\mid\mathcal{G}_{1}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{G}_{1}]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[Y\mid\mathcal{G}_{2}]\mid\mathcal{G}_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">In our derivation, <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is the product <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math>. We set <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{1}=\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{1}=\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and choose <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{2}=\sigma(D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T),\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{2}=\sigma(D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T),\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. This specific choice of <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is made to ensure that <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable with respect to the inner conditioning set, allowing it to be factored out from the inner expectation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.I2.i1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The same logic applies to <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting these into the expression for <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(2p_{i^{*}}-1)(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(2p_{i^{*}}-1)(\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}])." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The terms <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> are conditional probabilities of <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> (a binary variable that is <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus, they both lie in the interval <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The maximum possible absolute difference between any two values in this interval is <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-0=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-0=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|\leq|2p_{i}-1|\cdot 1=|2p_{i}-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|\leq|2p_{i}-1|\cdot 1=|2p_{i}-1|</annotation></semantics></math>. We set <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=|2p_{i}-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=|2p_{i}-1|</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="Sx1.I2.i1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq|2p_{i}-1|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq|2p_{i}-1|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">If <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to agent <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=T</annotation></semantics></math>:</span>
In this scenario, <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math>, the actual private choice of agent <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> at the final time step <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. When this outcome is revealed at step <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, it directly determines the value of <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> for agent <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> is already determined by information up to time <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math>, making it <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable).
Specifically:</p>
<ul id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain: <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=V_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k}]=V_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> (and thus <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math>) is now known given <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain:</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[X_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[X_{i^{*},T}\mid\mathcal{H}_{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(2p_{i^{*}}-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(2p_{i^{*}}-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This holds because <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable, and <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> by the independence of task <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> from past tasks.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=V_{i^{*},T}-D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(2p_{i^{*}}-1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=V_{i^{*},T}-D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(2p_{i^{*}}-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i^{*},T}=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i^{*},T}=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex78.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}-D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(2p_{i^{*}}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot X_{i^{*},T}-D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(2p_{i^{*}}-1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(X_{i^{*},T}-(2p_{i^{*}}-1))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)\cdot(X_{i^{*},T}-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the two possible values of <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math> holds.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{vote},i^{*}}(T)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=X_{i^{*},T}-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=X_{i^{*},T}-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}\in\{-1,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}\in\{-1,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i^{*}}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i^{*}}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=1-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)=2-2p_{i}=2(1-p_{i^{*}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=1-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)=2-2p_{i}=2(1-p_{i^{*}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i^{*},T}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i^{*},T}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}=-1-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)=-2p_{i^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}=-1-(2p_{i^{*}}-1)=-2p_{i^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The maximum absolute value of these terms is <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(2(1-p_{i^{*}}),2p_{i^{*}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(2(1-p_{i^{*}}),2p_{i^{*}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which occurs at <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i^{*}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i^{*}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i^{*}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i^{*}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and is equal to <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.I2.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{k}|\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{k}|\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Sx1.I2.i2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">We set <math id="Sx1.I2.i2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we calculate the sum of squares of these bounds over all <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="NT" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NT</annotation></semantics></math> events. We can group terms based on whether the private outcome <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> occurred before time <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>) or at time <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=T</annotation></semantics></math>).
Let <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{&lt;T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{&lt;T}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of indices <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> where the corresponding time <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{=T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{=T}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of indices <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> where the corresponding time <math id="Sx1.SS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}=T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in K_{&lt;T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in K_{&lt;T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we established that the bound <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=|2p_{i}-1|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=|2p_{i}-1|</annotation></semantics></math>. There are <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T-1)</annotation></semantics></math> time steps (from <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T-1</annotation></semantics></math>) for each of the <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> agents where this case applies. So, there are <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(T-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(T-1)</annotation></semantics></math> such terms.
For <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in K_{=T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in K_{=T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we established that the bound <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=2</annotation></semantics></math>. This case applies for each of the <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> agents at the final time step <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math>. So, there are <math id="Sx1.SS2.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> such terms.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">The sum of squares of these bounds over all <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="NT" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NT</annotation></semantics></math> events is therefore:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{k\in K_{&lt;T}}c_{k}^{2}+\sum_{k\in K_{=T}}c_{k}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{k\in K_{&lt;T}}c_{k}^{2}+\sum_{k\in K_{=T}}c_{k}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting the derived bounds for <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{N}2^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{N}2^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p13.3" class="ltx_p">In the first sum, for each agent <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the term <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2p_{i}-1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2p_{i}-1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> appears <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T-1)</annotation></semantics></math> times (once for each time step from <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math>). In the second sum, for each agent <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the term <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{2}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{2}=4</annotation></semantics></math> appears once (for the final time step <math id="Sx1.SS2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>). This simplifies to:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{NT}c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Proof for the Hallucination Bound.</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this proof, we utilize the upper-tail variant of the Azuma-Hoeffding inequality, restating Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Azuma-Hoeffding inequality []). ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> from above <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Sx1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{k})_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{k})_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be a martingale difference sequence w.r.t. <math id="Sx1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Sx1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{k}|\leq c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{k}|\leq c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> a.s. for all <math id="Sx1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="Sx1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(\sum_{k=1}^{K}Z_{k}\geq\epsilon\right)\ \leq\ \exp\!\left(-\frac{\epsilon^{2}}{2\sum_{k=1}^{K}c_{k}^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\!\left(\sum_{k=1}^{K}Z_{k}\geq\epsilon\right)\ \leq\ \exp\!\left(-\frac{\epsilon^{2}}{2\sum_{k=1}^{K}c_{k}^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For this derivation, we condition on <math id="Sx1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}={\omega_{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}={\omega_{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math>. From Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Azuma-Hoeffding inequality []). ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we obtain the following derivation:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\omega_{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\omega_{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}&gt;0\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}&gt;0\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Sx1.Ex85.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">We subtract <math id="Sx1.Ex85.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> from both sides.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{\omega_{\dagger}}\!\left({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\;\geq\;-\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{\omega_{\dagger}}\!\left({V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}-\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\;\geq\;-\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Sx1.Ex87.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">Apply the (upper-tail) Azuma–Hoeffding bound with <math id="Sx1.Ex87.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=-\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=-\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.Ex87.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}=D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}=D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Sx1.Ex88.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">and <math id="Sx1.Ex88.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum c_{k}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq e^{\left(-\frac{\big(\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\big)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.400em" minsize="2.400em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.400em" minsize="2.400em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.400em" minsize="2.400em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="2.400em" minsize="2.400em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq e^{\left(-\frac{\big(\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]\big)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Sx1.Ex90.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">Substitute the expected total net public vote under <math id="Sx1.Ex90.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}={\omega_{\dagger}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}={\omega_{\dagger}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"> <span id="Sx1.Ex91.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="Sx1.Ex91.m1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[V_{i,T}]=-\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">†</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">†</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">V</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ω</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">†</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">D</mi><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">vote</mtext><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[{V}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}_{T}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[V_{i,T}]=-\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{\left(-\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]\right)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.500em" minsize="0.500em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.400em" minsize="2.400em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="2.400em" minsize="2.400em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{\left(-\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\,\mathbb{E}_{\omega_{\dagger}}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]\right)^{2}}{2\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Proof for Theorem 3.</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As before, we condition on the final task’s true state <math id="Sx1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{T}=\omega^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{T}=\omega^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="Sx1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\cdot):=\mathbb{P}(\cdot\mid\Omega_{T}=\omega^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}(\cdot):=\mathbb{P}(\cdot\mid\Omega_{T}=\omega^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly. Recall the one-sided Azuma–Hoeffding lower bound derived in Equation <a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We seek to show that as <math id="Sx1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability of a correct majority converges to 1.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We recall the underlying parameters: <math id="Sx1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}V_{i,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}V_{i,T}</annotation></semantics></math> is the final net vote, <math id="Sx1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is agent <math id="Sx1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s distribution-level reliability, and <math id="Sx1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the publication decision. The term <math id="Sx1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2p_{i}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2p_{i}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the agent’s expected margin.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Sx1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n:=T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n:=T-1</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of learning rounds. The agent’s decision to publish at time <math id="Sx1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the number of correct predictions <math id="Sx1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> observed during learning.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To prove convergence, we proceed in <span id="Sx1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">four</span> steps:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(i) establish that the number of successes <math id="Sx1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a Binomial distribution;
(ii) show that the confidence <math id="Sx1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,T}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing in <math id="Sx1.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, implying the publish rule is a <span id="Sx1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">success-count threshold</span>;
(iii) bound the expected publish probability and vote margin using the uniform non-degeneracy assumption;
(iv) apply these bounds to the Azuma-Hoeffding result to show exponential convergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 1: Distribution of Successes.</span>
Under the <span id="Sx1.SS4.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">distribution-level reliability</span> definition, the outcomes of the <math id="Sx1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> learning tasks are i.i.d. Bernoulli(<math id="Sx1.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) trials. Thus, for any agent <math id="Sx1.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the success count <math id="Sx1.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a binomial distribution:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}\sim\mathrm{Binomial}(n,p_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Binomial</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}\sim\mathrm{Binomial}(n,p_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 2: Monotonicity and Threshold Rule.</span>
After observing <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}=k</annotation></semantics></math> successes, the posterior is <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,T}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(\alpha_{i,0}+k,\ \beta_{i,0}+n-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,T}\sim\mathrm{Beta}(\alpha_{i,0}+k,\ \beta_{i,0}+n-k)</annotation></semantics></math>. The agent publishes if its confidence <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(k):=\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,T}&gt;p_{\mathrm{critical},i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(k):=\mathbb{P}(\Psi_{i,T}&gt;p_{\mathrm{critical},i})</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a fixed critical threshold <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the regularized incomplete beta function <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{x}(\alpha,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing in <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and increasing in <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Since observing more successes (<math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>) increases <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and decreases <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, the tail probability <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(k)=1-I_{p_{\mathrm{critical},i}}(\dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(k)=1-I_{p_{\mathrm{critical},i}}(\dots)</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly non-decreasing in <math id="Sx1.SS4.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the condition <math id="Sx1.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(k)&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(k)&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math> defines a <span id="Sx1.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">success-count threshold</span>: there exists some <math id="Sx1.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the agent publishes if and only if <math id="Sx1.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}\geq k_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}\geq k_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 3: Bounding the Publish Probability.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We define the publish probability for agent <math id="Sx1.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of their competence <math id="Sx1.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}(p):=\mathbb{P}(K_{i}\geq k_{i}^{\star}\mid p)=\sum_{k=k_{i}^{\star}}^{n}\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}(p):=\mathbb{P}(K_{i}\geq k_{i}^{\star}\mid p)=\sum_{k=k_{i}^{\star}}^{n}\binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convergence)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix the horizon <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and the gate parameters (<math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0},\beta_{0},p_{\mathrm{crit}},\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>crit</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0},\beta_{0},p_{\mathrm{crit}},\tau</annotation></semantics></math>). Consider a sequence of agents <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying two conditions:</span></p>
<ol id="Sx1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Average Competence:</span><span id="Sx1.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The average reliability exceeds </span><math id="Sx1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Sx1.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by a margin </span><math id="Sx1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Sx1.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\geq\frac{1}{2}+\Delta p." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\geq\frac{1}{2}+\Delta p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Uniform Non-degeneracy:</span><span id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The gate is uniformly nondegenerate, meaning there exists a lower bound </span><math id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\min}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\min}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all agents </span><math id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and all </span><math id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the probability of publishing is at least </span><math id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (i.e., </span><math id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{i}q_{i}(p_{i})\geq q_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{i}q_{i}(p_{i})\geq q_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Sx1.I3.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for competent agents).</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, as <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}\!\big(V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}&gt;0\big)\ \geq\ 1-\exp\!\left(-\frac{2\,\Delta p^{2}\,q_{\min}^{\,2}}{T+3}\,N\right)\ \xrightarrow{}\ 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}\!\big(V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}&gt;0\big)\ \geq\ 1-\exp\!\left(-\frac{2\,\Delta p^{2}\,q_{\min}^{\,2}}{T+3}\,N\right)\ \xrightarrow{}\ 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the exponent from the Azuma-Hoeffding lower bound (Eq. <a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). We analyze the numerator and denominator separately.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Denominator:<span id="Sx1.SS4.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The variance term for each agent is bounded by <math id="Sx1.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\leq(T-1)+4=T+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\leq(T-1)+4=T+3</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over <math id="Sx1.SS4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> agents:</span></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}c_{i}^{2}\leq N(T+3)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}c_{i}^{2}\leq N(T+3).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Numerator:<span id="Sx1.SS4.p13.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The expected collective vote is <math id="Sx1.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="Sx1.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]=q_{i}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]=q_{i}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We split the sum into competent (<math id="Sx1.SS4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>) and incompetent (<math id="Sx1.SS4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>) agents.
For incompetent agents, <math id="Sx1.SS4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2p_{i}-1)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2p_{i}-1)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so their contribution to the sum is negative (or zero).
For competent agents, we use the uniform non-degeneracy assumption: <math id="Sx1.SS4.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}(p_{i})\geq q_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}(p_{i})\geq q_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus:</span></span></p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N}(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex96.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i:p_{i}\geq 1/2}(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}(p_{i})+\sum_{i:p_{i}&lt;1/2}(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i:p_{i}\geq 1/2}(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}(p_{i})+\sum_{i:p_{i}&lt;1/2}(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq q_{\min}\sum_{i:p_{i}\geq 1/2}(2p_{i}-1)+\sum_{i:p_{i}&lt;1/2}(2p_{i}-1)\cdot 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq q_{\min}\sum_{i:p_{i}\geq 1/2}(2p_{i}-1)+\sum_{i:p_{i}&lt;1/2}(2p_{i}-1)\cdot 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Sx1.Ex98.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">(Since <math id="Sx1.Ex98.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and terms are negative, replacing <math id="Sx1.Ex98.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with 1 lowers the sum)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=q_{\min}\left(\sum_{i:p_{i}\geq 1/2}(2p_{i}-1)+\sum_{i:p_{i}&lt;1/2}(2p_{i}-1)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q_{\min}\left(\sum_{i:p_{i}\geq 1/2}(2p_{i}-1)+\sum_{i:p_{i}&lt;1/2}(2p_{i}-1)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="Sx1.Ex100.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="font-size:70%;">(Assuming <math id="Sx1.Ex100.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\min}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\min}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can factor it out safely)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2q_{\min}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(p_{i}-1/2)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2q_{\min}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(p_{i}-1/2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the average competence assumption <math id="Sx1.SS4.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum(p_{i}-1/2)=N(\bar{p}-1/2)\geq N\Delta p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum(p_{i}-1/2)=N(\bar{p}-1/2)\geq N\Delta p</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Numerator}\geq 2q_{\min}N\Delta p." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Numerator</mtext><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Numerator}\geq 2q_{\min}N\Delta p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 4: Convergence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these into the Azuma-Hoeffding bound:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}&gt;1-\exp\left(-\frac{(2q_{\min}N\Delta p)^{2}}{2\cdot N(T+3)}\right)=1-\exp\left(-\frac{2\Delta p^{2}q_{\min}^{2}}{T+3}N\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\omega}^{*}&gt;1-\exp\left(-\frac{(2q_{\min}N\Delta p)^{2}}{2\cdot N(T+3)}\right)=1-\exp\left(-\frac{2\Delta p^{2}q_{\min}^{2}}{T+3}N\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS4.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="Sx1.SS4.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta p,q_{\min}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta p,q_{\min}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, the exponent grows linearly with <math id="Sx1.SS4.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, driving the error probability to 0.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Pseudocode for Empirical Evaluation.</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the framework using three routines: a per–agent
gate-and-contribution calculator (Alg. 1), a lower bound aggregator (Alg. 2),
and a Monte–Carlo simulator of the full sequential process (Alg. 3).</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We vary a single control parameter (e.g. <math id="Sx1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>abstain</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}</annotation></semantics></math>) while
keeping the others fixed, and report <span id="Sx1.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">four</span> scenarios: (i) homogeneous agents (<math id="Sx1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\equiv 0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\equiv 0.55</annotation></semantics></math>);
(ii) heterogeneous with abstention (half <math id="Sx1.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.35</annotation></semantics></math>, half <math id="Sx1.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>); (iii) the same heterogeneous
pool with abstention disabled; and (iv) heterogeneous with <span id="Sx1.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">contrary (competence-inverse) priors</span>
used during learning. For each setting we plot the probabilistic lower bound from
Algs. 1–2 alongside the Monte–Carlo estimate from Alg. 3. Consistently, the gate filters
low-competence agents, increasing the expected margin and tightening the lower bound; both
empirical success and the certificate improve with larger <math id="Sx1.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contrary priors (used in scenario (iv)).</h4>

<div id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For agent <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with true reliability <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we set the Beta prior mean to <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with strength <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and we clip Beta pseudo–counts below by <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for numerical stability:</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,0}\ :=\ \max\!\big(\kappa(1-p_{i}),\,\varepsilon\big),\qquad\beta_{i,0}\ :=\ \max\!\big(\kappa p_{i},\,\varepsilon\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,0}\ :=\ \max\!\big(\kappa(1-p_{i}),\,\varepsilon\big),\qquad\beta_{i,0}\ :=\ \max\!\big(\kappa p_{i},\,\varepsilon\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so competent agents start pessimistic and weak agents optimistic. (When not using contrary priors
we employ aligned, shared priors <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{0},\beta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{0},\beta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> for all agents.)
For instance, with <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=8</annotation></semantics></math> and a competent agent <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>, we set</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,0}=\kappa(1-p_{i})=8\cdot 0.25=2,\qquad\beta_{i,0}=\kappa p_{i}=8\cdot 0.75=6," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,0}=\kappa(1-p_{i})=8\cdot 0.25=2,\qquad\beta_{i,0}=\kappa p_{i}=8\cdot 0.75=6,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">so the prior <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Beta}(2,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Beta}(2,6)</annotation></semantics></math> is pessimistic despite <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}&gt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}&gt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Conversely, for a weak agent <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=0.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=0.35</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="Sx1.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,0}=8\cdot(1-0.35)=5.2,\qquad\beta_{i,0}=8\cdot 0.35=2.8," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.35</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>5.2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.35</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2.8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,0}=8\cdot(1-0.35)=5.2,\qquad\beta_{i,0}=8\cdot 0.35=2.8,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">yielding an optimistic prior <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Beta}(5.2,2.8)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Beta}(5.2,2.8)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alg. 1 (AgentGateAndContribution).</span>
Fix horizon <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=T-1</annotation></semantics></math> learning rounds), agent <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s prior
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})</annotation></semantics></math> (aligned or contrary), competence <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, target level <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{critical},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{critical},i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and abstention threshold <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The routine enumerates all learning histories with <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> correct private
outcomes. For each <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> it forms the posterior <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Beta}(\alpha_{i,0}+k,\beta_{i,0}+n-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Beta}(\alpha_{i,0}+k,\beta_{i,0}+n-k)</annotation></semantics></math>
and computes the agent’s <span id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">confidence</span>
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,T}=1-I_{p_{\mathrm{critical},i}}(\alpha_{i,0}+k,\beta_{i,0}+n-k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,T}=1-I_{p_{\mathrm{critical},i}}(\alpha_{i,0}+k,\beta_{i,0}+n-k)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i,T}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math> (or if publishing is forced), that
history counts as “publish”. Weighting by the binomial likelihood
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{n}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{n}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math> and summing over <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> yields
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability that agent <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> will
<span id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">publish</span> at time <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> under the model. Multiplying by the margin <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2p_{i}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2p_{i}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> gives
the agent’s expected contribution <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to the final net vote. The update
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\leftarrow q_{i}+\mathbf{1}\{\text{publish at }k\}\binom{n}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>publish at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\leftarrow q_{i}+\mathbf{1}\{\text{publish at }k\}\binom{n}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math>
implements the law of total probability:</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\ast}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>vote</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\ast}[D_{\mathrm{vote},i}(T)]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n}\underbrace{\mathbf{1}\{\mathcal{C}_{i,T}(k)&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}\}}_{\mathbb{P}(\text{publish}\mid K_{i}=k)}\underbrace{\binom{n}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{n-k}}_{\mathbb{P}(K_{i}=k)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>publish</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n}\underbrace{\mathbf{1}\{\mathcal{C}_{i,T}(k)&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}\}}_{\mathbb{P}(\text{publish}\mid K_{i}=k)}\underbrace{\binom{n}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{n-k}}_{\mathbb{P}(K_{i}=k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">that is, we add the probability of each history that would vote publicly.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>AgentGateAndContribution<math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In :</span> <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,\,\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0},\,p_{i},\,p_{\mathrm{critical},i},\,\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,\,\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0},\,p_{i},\,p_{\mathrm{critical},i},\,\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="algorithm1.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">force<math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Out :</span> <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\ast}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mtext>vote</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\ast}[D_{\text{vote},i}(T)]</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=(2p_{i}-1)\,q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=(2p_{i}-1)\,q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leftarrow T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leftarrow T-1</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\_\mathrm{post}\leftarrow\alpha_{i,0}+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>post</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\_\mathrm{post}\leftarrow\alpha_{i,0}+k</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\_\mathrm{post}\leftarrow\beta_{i,0}+n-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>post</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\_\mathrm{post}\leftarrow\beta_{i,0}+n-k</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{conf}\leftarrow 1-\mathrm{BetaCDF}\!\big(p_{\mathrm{critical},i};\,\alpha\_\mathrm{post},\beta\_\mathrm{post}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>conf</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:4.418em;" width="4.418em"><mi>BetaCDF</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>critical</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>post</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>post</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{conf}\leftarrow 1-\mathrm{BetaCDF}\!\big(p_{\mathrm{critical},i};\,\alpha\_\mathrm{post},\beta\_\mathrm{post}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{publish}\leftarrow(\texttt{force}=1)\ \lor\ (\text{conf}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>publish</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">force</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>conf</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>abstain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{publish}\leftarrow(\texttt{force}=1)\ \lor\ (\text{conf}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain},i})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\leftarrow q_{i}+\mathbf{1}\{\text{publish}\}\,\binom{n}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>publish</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\leftarrow q_{i}+\mathbf{1}\{\text{publish}\}\,\binom{n}{k}p_{i}^{k}(1-p_{i})^{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}\leftarrow(2p_{i}-1)\,q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}\leftarrow(2p_{i}-1)\,q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.10.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i},c_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i},c_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alg. 2 (BoundFromContrib).</span>
Given the per–agent contributions <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and competences <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the routine
computes the numerator <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{num}}=\sum_{i}c_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>num</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{num}}=\sum_{i}c_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}^{*}[V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}]</annotation></semantics></math>
and the Azuma–Hoeffding denominator
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{den}}=\sum_{i}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>den</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{den}}=\sum_{i}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, which collects the bounded
differences from the <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> learning reveals and the final private vote (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 4 Derivation and Simulation of Final Vote Accuracy Guarantees ‣ Epistemic Filtering and Collective Hallucination: A Jury Theorem for Confidence-Calibrated Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
It returns the lower bound
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1-\exp\!\big(-S_{\mathrm{num}}^{2}/(2S_{\mathrm{den}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>num</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>den</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\exp\!\big(-S_{\mathrm{num}}^{2}/(2S_{\mathrm{den}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math> on the probability
that the final majority is correct.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>BoundFromContrib</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In :</span> <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=(2p_{i}-1)q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Out :</span> <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LB}\ \approx\ \text{lower bound on }\mathbb{P}_{\ast}(V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>LB</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≈</mo><mrow><mtext>lower bound on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LB}\ \approx\ \text{lower bound on }\mathbb{P}_{\ast}(V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{num}}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>num</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{num}}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{den}}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>den</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{den}}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big((T-1)(2p_{i}-1)^{2}+4\big)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{LB}\leftarrow 1-\exp\!\big(-S_{\mathrm{num}}^{2}/(2S_{\mathrm{den}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>LB</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>num</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>den</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LB}\leftarrow 1-\exp\!\big(-S_{\mathrm{num}}^{2}/(2S_{\mathrm{den}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LB</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LB}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alg. 3 (MonteCarloEvaluate).</span>
This routine simulates the full process end-to-end. In each run it initializes all
agents with either a shared prior <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{0},\beta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{0},\beta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">or</span> per–agent priors
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})\}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., contrary priors as above), then executes <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> learning rounds.
In round <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, agent <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> draws a private outcome (correct with probability <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) and updates its Beta
counts accordingly. At the decision round <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, each agent computes its posterior
confidence <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-I_{p_{\mathrm{critical}}}(\alpha_{i},\beta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>critical</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-I_{p_{\mathrm{critical}}}(\alpha_{i},\beta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and publishes iff it
exceeds <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>abstain</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}</annotation></semantics></math> (or publishing is forced). Publishing agents then cast
a final private vote (<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math> w.p. <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise). The net vote is the sum of
published votes; a run is a <span id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">win</span> if the net number of votes is strictly positive. Repeating over
<math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> runs yields the empirical success rate, referred to as <math id="Sx1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{\mathrm{emp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>emp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{\mathrm{emp}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span>MonteCarloEvaluate</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm3.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In :</span> <math id="algorithm3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,T,\,p_{\mathrm{critical}},\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>critical</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>abstain</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,T,\,p_{\mathrm{critical}},\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}}</annotation></semantics></math>; list <math id="algorithm3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="algorithm3.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">force<math id="algorithm3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math></span>; runs <math id="algorithm3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>; 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Either</span> shared prior <math id="algorithm3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{0},\beta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{0},\beta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm3.4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">or</span> per–agent priors <math id="algorithm3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Out :</span> <math id="algorithm3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{\mathrm{emp}}(V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>emp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{\mathrm{emp}}(V_{T}^{\omega^{*}-{\omega_{\dagger}}}&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{wins}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>wins</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{wins}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="algorithm3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leftarrow T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leftarrow T-1</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1,\dots,R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1,\dots,R</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.4.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm3.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm3.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">learning phase  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm3.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.7.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.4.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i},\beta_{i})\leftarrow\begin{cases}(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})&amp;\text{if per\textendash agent priors given}\\
(\alpha_{0},\beta_{0})&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>if per–agent priors given</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i},\beta_{i})\leftarrow\begin{cases}(\alpha_{i,0},\beta_{i,0})&amp;\text{if per\textendash agent priors given}\\
(\alpha_{0},\beta_{0})&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm3.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.4.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm3.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.10.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.4.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="algorithm3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i},\beta_{i})\leftarrow(\alpha_{i}+1,\beta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i},\beta_{i})\leftarrow(\alpha_{i}+1,\beta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="algorithm3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s{=}1</annotation></semantics></math> else <math id="algorithm3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{i},\beta_{i}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{i},\beta_{i}+1)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm3.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm3.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">decision phase  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{net}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>net</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{net}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm3.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.14.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.4.14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{conf}\leftarrow 1-\mathrm{BetaCDF}\!\big(p_{\mathrm{critical}};\alpha_{i},\beta_{i}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>conf</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:4.418em;" width="4.418em"><mi>BetaCDF</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>critical</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{conf}\leftarrow 1-\mathrm{BetaCDF}\!\big(p_{\mathrm{critical}};\alpha_{i},\beta_{i}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{publish}\leftarrow(\texttt{force}=1)\ \lor\ (\text{conf}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>publish</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">force</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>conf</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>abstain</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{publish}\leftarrow(\texttt{force}=1)\ \lor\ (\text{conf}&gt;\tau_{\mathrm{abstain}})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
